Description: pvr: report a 128 MiB maxUniformBufferRange
 maxUniformBufferRange is a literal 16 KiB, the Vulkan 1.0 minimum. Before
 a22ad99bdd2 ("pvr: set device features/props/extensions to Vulkan 1.0
 minimums (unless implemented)") it was 128 MiB. Uniform and storage buffers
 take the same path: both use nir_address_format_vec2_index_32bit_offset
 (pco_nir.c), both are lowered by trans_load_buffer() (pco_trans_nir.c),
 which adds a 32-bit offset to the 64-bit address from the buffer
 descriptor, and the descriptor holds a 32-bit size (struct
 pvr_buffer_descriptor, pvr_common.h). Only inline uniform blocks are read
 from shared registers, and they have their own limits.
 .
 Report the same range as maxStorageBufferRange. zink clamps every bound
 uniform buffer to maxUniformBufferRange (zink_context.c) and derives
 GL_MAX_UNIFORM_BLOCK_SIZE from it; wgpu reports it as
 max_uniform_buffer_binding_size.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
